      {
        "id": "btn-ln-4",
        "name": "Ema Datshi (Chili Cheese Stew)",
        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "servings": 4,
        "prepTime": 10,
        "cookTime": 20,
        "ingredients": [
          "10-12 large green chilies (or mix of green and red)",
          "200g Bhutanese datshi cheese (or a mix of feta and mozzarella)",
          "1 tomato (quartered)",
          "1 onion (sliced)",
          "2 tbsp butter",
          "Water",
          "Salt"
        ],
        "instructions": [
          "Slice chilies lengthwise — keep seeds for heat",
          "Sauté onion in butter briefly",
          "Add chilies and tomato, stir",
          "Add enough water to barely cover",
          "Simmer 10-15 minutes until chilies soften",
          "Add cheese in chunks — stir until melted into a thick, spicy sauce",
          "Do NOT make it smooth — it should be chunky with visible chili pieces",
          "Season with salt",
          "Serve with red rice — the national meal of Bhutan",
          "This is not a side dish — it IS the main dish, and the chili is a vegetable, not a condiment"
        ],
        "description": "Bhutan's national dish — a stew where chilies are the main ingredient, not a seasoning. Cheese melted into a fiery, chunky sauce served over red rice. Went viral when travel food creators discovered that Bhutanese people eat more chili per capita than anywhere else on Earth.",
